PP layer-range parametrization of the decoder TC tile functions (#25 phase-2, Lane C)

WHAT: dectc_forward_tile / dectc_backward_tile gain `template <int Llo = 0,
int Lhi = dec::kLayers>` + fp32 boundary-adjoint args (dh_in/dh_out, default
nullptr), realizing the design §4.1 PP stage cut:
  * Llo>0  skips the embedding (X_in[Llo] = upstream stage's handoff in acts)
           and writes the final running adjoint to dh_out (fp32 [T,d]) instead
           of the bf16 dh0;
  * Lhi<kLayers skips head/CE (returns 0 NLL; the boundary layer's n2 output
           goes to X_in[Lhi] via the existing li+1<kLayers branch) and seeds
           the backward's running adjoint from dh_in (fp32 [T,d]).
The fp32 dh carrier is bit-preserving: in the fused path the inter-layer
adjoint never rounds to bf16, so a PP stage composition can be BIT-IDENTICAL
to the single-launch kernel (gated by tests/hw/test_pp2_loopback_determinism.py).

DEFAULT-INSTANTIATION IDENTITY (design §1.2 discipline): every existing call
site compiles unchanged (all-defaulted template params); PTX of the production
<OptId::AdamW> wgmma megakernel instantiation was diffed patched-vs-unpatched
on 2026-06-12: 16,543 lines each, sole delta = one `mov.u32 %r3655, 0;`
scheduled one line earlier (same instruction, same register — scheduling
jitter, zero semantic delta). SG_DECTC_LAYER_RANGE 1 is the patch-presence
marker pp_stage_decoder_tc.cuh #errors on and the PP tests skip-loudly on.

APPLY:  git apply .phase2/patches/0001-dectc-layer-range-pp.patch
VERIFY: nvcc-compile mega_decoder_real_adamw_tc.cu (proven 2026-06-12, shadow
        tree) + the PTX diff above; then run the PP runbook entries.

